@@ -0,0 +1,75 @@
+# SOLUTION
+
+`make test` was failing for four independent environment/config problems left by the
+botched merge. No Python source and nothing under `tests/` was changed, and no check,
+target, or validation step was removed — `make test` still runs `check` (config
+validation) followed by the full pytest suite.
+
+The four failures were serial: each one masked the next, so they only surfaced one at a
+time as each was fixed.
+
+## 1. `Makefile` — recipe indented with spaces instead of a tab
+
+**Symptom:** `Makefile:4: *** missing separator.  Stop.` (exit 2)
+
+The `test:` recipe line was indented with 4 spaces. Make requires a literal tab to
+introduce a recipe line. The `check:` recipe below it still had its tab, which is the
+tell-tale sign of an editor/merge mangling only the conflicting hunk.
+
+**Fix:** Re-indented `python3 -m pytest -q tests/` with a tab.
+
+## 2. `scripts/run_checks.sh` — lost its executable bit
+
+**Symptom:** `make: ./scripts/run_checks.sh: Permission denied` (exit 127)
+
+The file was mode `100644`, but the `check` target invokes it directly as
+`./scripts/run_checks.sh`. Git records the executable bit, and the merge brought the
+file back as non-executable.
+
+**Fix:** `chmod +x scripts/run_checks.sh` (now mode `100755`, which git has picked up
+as a mode change in the working tree).
+
+## 3. `scripts/run_checks.sh` — CRLF line endings
+
+**Symptom:** `make: ./scripts/run_checks.sh: No such file or directory` (exit 127) —
+confusing, because the file plainly existed and was by then executable.
+
+The file came from the other machine with Windows CRLF terminators. The shebang was
+therefore `#!/bin/bash\r`, so the kernel looked for an interpreter literally named
+`/bin/bash\r`, which does not exist. The "No such file or directory" refers to the
+interpreter, not the script.
+
+**Fix:** Converted the file to LF endings. I scanned every tracked file for CR bytes;
+this was the only one affected.
+
+## 4. `data/config.json` — trailing comma makes it invalid JSON
+
+**Symptom:** `json.decoder.JSONDecodeError: Expecting property name enclosed in double
+quotes: line 5 column 1`, so `tools/validate_config.py` exited non-zero and failed the
+`check` target.
+
+`"batch_size": 500,` had a trailing comma before the closing brace. That is legal in
+several config dialects but not in strict JSON.
+
+**Fix:** Removed the trailing comma. The config's actual values were fine — validation
+now reports `config ok: data/config.json`.
+
+## Verification
+
+```
+$ make test
+./scripts/run_checks.sh
+config ok: data/config.json
+all checks passed
+python3 -m pytest -q tests/
+...                                                                      [100%]
+3 passed in 0.01s
+EXIT=0
+```
+
+## Note
+
+Two of these (the executable bit and the CRLF endings) will come back the next time
+someone merges from that machine. Adding a `.gitattributes` with `*.sh text eol=lf`
+would pin the line endings repo-wide and prevent a recurrence. I did not add one, as it
+was outside the scope of getting `make test` passing.
